  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Humanitarian Assistance for Vulnerable Populations in Gaza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian situation in the Occupied Palestinian Territory continues to deteriorate. Nearly 90 per cent of Gaza&#x2019;s population &#x2013; approximately 1.9 million people &#x2013; have been displaced, over half of them children. People have been forced to move repeatedly, leaving possessions behind as homes, services and community infrastructure are largely destroyed. Lacking access to safe, private or dignified shelter, families are living in makeshift shelters, tents or even outdoors. Access to essential life-sustaining services, including hospitals and clinics, and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) systems, is severely limited.IOM aims at addressing the ongoing humanitarian crisis in Gaza by implementing a multi-sectoral approach designed to address acute shelter, WASH, and site management needs. These interventions aim to enhance operational capacity while ensuring that displaced populations have access to safe, dignified shelter and essential services. IOM is also strengthening logistical networks, pre-position supplies and support local actors to ensure timely delivery of aid.</narrative>
  </description>
